    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5f7c97a3_976a68e9",
        "filename": "keystone/limit/models/strict_two_level.py",
        "patchSetId": 17
      },
      "lineNbr": 82,
      "author": {
        "id": 5046
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-07-09T20:26:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This method and the next method seem to really just wrap the really model logic in _check_limit().\n\nI wonder if it wouldn\u0027t be more clear to just define a single method as the interface called check_limit() instead of two separate methods that require a private method to reduce duplication. Then the logic in limit/core.py builds standardizes whatever is passed into check_limit() regardless of create or update requests.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 82,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 82,
        "endChar": 38
      },
      "revId": "4bb3604663beb7ba9cc9280df06dd0c7b08a3cb7",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5f7c97a3_ba15049d",
        "filename": "keystone/limit/models/strict_two_level.py",
        "patchSetId": 17
      },
      "lineNbr": 82,
      "author": {
        "id": 15054
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-07-10T03:38:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "the input parameters for create and update request is different. create request input is a list for limits, the update request input is a single limit and a specified limit_id, so I separate them and let them both use _check_limit for hierarchy check.\n\nThey can be merged into one of cause,but I\u0027m not sure how to make the common one more generic for input parameters. Any suggestion?",
      "parentUuid": "5f7c97a3_976a68e9",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 82,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 82,
        "endChar": 38
      },
